elds.\n2. Freeze 36 source groups before constructing candidates. Use 18 train,\n   six calibration, and 12 held-out groups. No source group may cross a\n   split. Record the manifest and hash before opening candidate labels.\n3. Construct one exact positive mapping per group from the executable\n   specification. Construct one negative by applying exactly one frozen\n   fault: bound change, coefficient swap, objective-direction reversal, or\n   constraint omission. Preserve all attempted mutations.\n4. Run Z3 and bounded enumeration on both candidates. Require agreement on\n   domain, satisfiability, optimum, objective order, and solution-space\n   relation. Unknown, timeout, disagreement, or multiple faults rejects the\n   pair without replacement from the held-out split.\n5. Alpha-rename identifiers and canonicalize harmless formatting through a\n   label-blind function. Randomize pair order from the frozen seed. Keep the\n   unblinded source and mutation fields outside the future feature table.\n6. Write raw candidate rows and exact authority rows before aggregate\n   metrics. Each split must contain both labels. The held-out split must\n   cover all four fault families and all three formulation families.\n7. Set contrast_fixture_complete_score=1 only when all 36 pairs are\n   terminal, both authorities agree, and every hash replays. Set\n   label_balance_ready_score=1 only when each split is exactly balanced,\n   source-disjoint, and nonconstant.\n8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,\n   adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.\n9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific\n   principle per required field and both contrast_fixture_complete_score\n   and label_balance_ready_score; preconditions_checked;\n   inference_substrate (deterministic_z3_contrast_fixture_no_llm);\n   duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; source_manifest_rows;\n   source_manifest_hash; rows; per_pair_results;