ed journals, and no current or future label in the event\n   view. On failure, write blocked_per_knot_continuous_learning with\n   gate_check_summary. External absence is blocked, not partial.\n1. Add REQ-LEARN-6991 and RED tests before implementation. Cover arm\n   isolation, pre-label selection, post-outcome updates, active-knot support,\n   importance anchoring, zero-advantage no-op, journal replay, rollback,\n   matched budgets, future-label denial, and bare downstream fields.\n2. Freeze arm order rotation, initial checkpoint, event order, feature\n   schema, pairwise loss, learning rate, knot budget, importance rule,\n   retention window, rollback threshold, and state-size budget before event\n   one. Do not load any GGUF or mutate model weights.\n3. Start four arms from the same checkpoint: frozen; unrestricted online\n   pairwise SGD; uniform importance anchoring; and per-knot importance\n   anchoring. Give every arm the same candidate features and compute budget.\n4. At event t, expose only the visibility manifest through t-1. Each arm\n   scores candidates and durably records its selection before the sealed\n   exact outcome opens.\n5. After outcome, compute exact group advantage. Apply the preregistered\n   pairwise direction for positive or negative advantage. Apply no update\n   for all-valid and all-invalid tied groups. Never use model confidence as\n   update or release authority.\n6. For the per-knot arm, update only splines whose compact support is active\n   on the event. Scale anchoring by accumulated knot importance. Journal\n   prepare, coefficient delta, certificate digest, commit, abort, and state\n   hash for every proposed update.\n7. After each committed update, replay only prior retention anchors. Roll\n   back if a prior exact success is lost, a PWA invariant fails, an inactive\n   knot changes, or the state budget is exceeded. Do not inspect future\n   support for online rollback.\n8. After all events, open frozen held-future windows once